  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607184900: Serialized component bridge scratch qualification

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Decision

One linked provider owns one isolated 64 KiB bridge page. Every call using that
page is serialized across consumer instances, pointer arguments are rewritten
into the page, and declared buffers alone are copied. A layout exceeding the
page is rejected before the provider export is invoked. Executable evidence
runs sixteen independent consumers concurrently through one provider and also
exercises the 65,537-byte rejection boundary.

## Maturity boundary

This establishes memory isolation and deterministic shared-scratch behavior for
the JVM prototype. It is not a throughput claim, a formal linear-memory proof,
or evidence for distributed providers or a browser SharedArrayBuffer bridge.")))
